| `transports.extras.<transport>` | string | `rest` `transport`; `grpc` `grpc` when the copier answer `transports` keeps grpc | a transport name mapped to one `pyproject.toml` optional extra, a word with no spaces; `{}` when absent | `scripts/check_venv.py`; `tests/optional_deps.py` | While the transport is in `transports.enabled`, `make check-venv` judges the extra's requirements and names it in the pip command, and a test that imports through `tests/optional_deps.py` with that surface fails instead of skipping on a missing package. An extra `pyproject.toml` does not declare is refused with exit 14; a surface `tests/optional_deps.py` `SURFACES` lacks is a test error. Absent, both write `[using default] transports.extras = {}` to stderr. | the gate's own tools: `venv.extras` | always |
